IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oasda-witnesses`
IMPORT `oasda-qa`

-- Oaths, Affidavits and Statutory Declarations Act 2005 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (oasda-qa.l4): every exported
-- question, for every role and every situation. Generated by the scratchpad script qa/b13/gen_oasda_cases.py; the
-- expected values were written by hand from the deposited text and are in that script.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it is an
-- assumed term"). Each question with the situation input is asked, for its own role, with the other document and
-- every later input ASSUMEd, and must answer `does not arise for you`. Where the situation holds, each question is
-- asked on facts worked by hand, and once against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. The two
-- questions for both roles have no role they are not about.
--
-- One limit (graffiti finding 31): the baseline reads `Place`, `Schedule 2 description` and `Kind of act` through
-- OTHERWISE, so for those an ASSUMEd value that is read would not be caught. The situation is read only through the
-- layer's helpers, which list every value.
--
-- Facts are the baseline's (oasda-cases-witnesses.l4): Daniel, a lawyer, d031 and d034.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked document` IS A `Document`
ASSUME `an unasked declaration` IS A `Statutory declaration`
ASSUME `an unasked declaration witness` IS A `Statutory declaration witness`
ASSUME `an unasked affidavit witness` IS A `Affidavit witness`
ASSUME `an unasked act` IS A `Kind of act`

`as the maker` MEANS `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit`
`as the witness` MEANS `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

`a declaration` MEANS `a statutory declaration`
`an affidavit made` MEANS `an affidavit`



