§§ `For the person making a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

§§§ `ss 5, 11, 12, 16 (situation: the document)`

-- May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit
-- s 5: anyone may affirm instead of swearing.
#ASSERT `May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` EQUALS `yes if` `May I affirm instead of swearing`
#ASSERT `May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit` `as the maker` `a declaration` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit` `as the witness` `an unasked document` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time
#ASSERT `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time` `as the maker` `a declaration` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time` `as the maker` `a declaration` EQUALS `yes if` `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter`
#ASSERT `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time` `as the witness` `an unasked document` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Is my statutory declaration valid
-- d034: Daniel's client before him: valid; the witness's name and qualification left off: not; the qualification left off but saved by s 16: valid; signed at home and posted: not.
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `a declaration` `Daniel's client declares before him in his office (d034)` EQUALS `my declaration is` `validly made under s 12`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `a declaration` `the witness forgot their name and qualification` EQUALS `my declaration is` `not validly made: the witness did not write their name and qualification`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `a declaration` `the witness forgot their qualification, saved by s 16` EQUALS `my declaration is` `valid despite a departure: s 16 saves it`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `a declaration` `signed at home and posted to the witness, no oral declaration` EQUALS `my declaration is` `not validly made: I did not declare orally in the witness's presence`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `a declaration` `signed at home and posted to the witness, no oral declaration` EQUALS `my declaration is` (`Is my statutory declaration validly made` `signed at home and posted to the witness, no oral declaration`)
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` `an unasked declaration` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration valid` `as the witness` `an unasked document` `an unasked declaration` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14, 15 (no situation input)`

-- Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document
-- Signed with a stamp: not admissible; in Vietnamese with no translation: not admissible; with a translator's affidavit: no bar.
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` `as the maker` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `for ss 14 and 15` `not admissible: signed with a rubber stamp (s 15(3))`
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` `as the maker` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `for ss 14 and 15` `not admissible: no English translation with a translator's affidavit (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` `as the maker` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `for ss 14 and 15` `ss 14 and 15 do not stand in the way`
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` `as the maker` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `for ss 14 and 15` (`Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting it` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` `as the witness` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Criminal Code s 169`

-- Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said
-- A knowingly false statement, false in a material particular: yes; true: no; false but not known to be: no.
#ASSERT `Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said` `as the maker` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said` `as the maker` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said` `as the maker` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I commit the false statement crime` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said` `as the witness` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement
-- A statutory declaration: 5 years, or summarily 2 years and $24 000; an affidavit: 7 years, or summarily 3 years and $36 000. The document is the question's fact, not a situation that can fail.
#ASSERT `What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement` `as the maker` `a declaration` EQUALS `the most is` (`Most I face` 5 2 24000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` EQUALS `the most is` (`Most I face` 7 3 36000)
#ASSERT `What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement` `as the maker` `an affidavit made` EQUALS `the most is` (`What is the most I face for a false statement` `my affidavit, sworn or affirmed`)
#ASSERT `What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement` `as the witness` `an unasked document` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

§§§ `Schedule 2, s 12(6) (situation: the document -- a statutory declaration)`

-- Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2
-- Admitted, with a practising certificate: a lawyer; admitted without one: still a lawyer (item 20); not admitted: not.
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the witness` `a declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the witness` `a declaration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the witness` `a declaration` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the witness` `a declaration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I a lawyer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the witness` `an affidavit made` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` `as the maker` `an unasked document` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- May I witness this statutory declaration, and how
-- d034: Daniel in Perth: Schedule 2; in Melbourne, as a Commonwealth witness (assumed); with neither: not; abroad in Italy: not; a London notary: yes.
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `a declaration` `Daniel, a lawyer, witnesses a client's declaration in Perth (d034)` EQUALS `as a witness of this declaration I am` `authorised: a person described in Schedule 2 (s 12(6)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `a declaration` `Daniel witnesses in Melbourne, a Commonwealth witness (assumed)` EQUALS `as a witness of this declaration I am` `authorised: a Commonwealth statutory declaration witness (s 12(6)(a)(ii) or (b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `a declaration` `Daniel witnesses in Melbourne, no Commonwealth or Victorian authority` EQUALS `as a witness of this declaration I am` `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `a declaration` `Daniel witnesses on holiday in Italy, with no local authority` EQUALS `as a witness of this declaration I am` `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `a declaration` `a London notary public witnesses` EQUALS `as a witness of this declaration I am` (`May I witness this statutory declaration` `a London notary public witnesses`)
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the witness` `an affidavit made` `an unasked declaration witness` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` `as the maker` `an unasked document` `an unasked declaration witness` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 9(6)-(8), 10(5) (situation: the document -- an affidavit)`

-- Am I an experienced legal practitioner for affidavits
